From bf8a3cb4ba668c3d00703dbd7a6e7afffabe7bfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:05:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] perf(kanban origin): look up only the projection's
 own cards instead of indexing every replica task key

_Publications answered "does another gateway publish this card?" for removed-owner obligations by pulling
every task key of every listed gateway into Python and indexing it. The replica now holds 25,511 task keys,
past the 25,000-key memo bound, so that ran on every linked-card projection; inside the busy Desktop backend
the one-row-at-a-time read was the largest part of a ~8 s projection (43 ms standalone), to answer ~18 rows.

Now project() passes the (board, task id) of its own obligations, and the first ask runs ONE query that
SQLite filters in C (exact "/<board>/<task>" suffix of 3-part keys, no LIKE/GLOB wildcards), returning only
those cards' rows. A card outside that set gets one exact lookup. Answers stay fixed per projection and
payloads stay live, as before. kanban_publication_index (the full-inventory memo) is removed; its tests are
rewritten against the same behaviors plus the one-query read.

Co-Authored-By: Contributor <contributor@example.com>
